In this exercise, I used the Azure portal to create a resource. The focus of the exercise is observing how Azure resource groups populate 
with created resources.

Task

1. Selected Create a resource > Compute > Virtual Machine > Create.
2. Verify or enter the following values for each setting. If a setting isn't specified, leave the default value.

Basics tab

Setting	Value
Subscription	AZ-900T00-A CSR 1
Resource group	myRGKV-lod59988255
Virtual machine name	my-VM-59988255
Image	Ubuntu Server 20.04 LTS - Gen2
Size	Click See all sizes, click B-Series, select B1ls, click Select at the bottom of the screen
Authentication type	Password
Username	azureuser
Password	Enter a custom password such as G*5e!pM0Djm0G*5e!pM0Djm0
Confirm password	Reenter the custom password
Public inbound ports	None

3. Review and create, It will take you to a billing tab where you will review your resource details and billing.
